Haiti creates national gambling regulator ANJHA to oversee casinos, betting and borlette

Haiti has set up the Autorité Nationale des Jeux de Hasard et d'Argent (ANJHA) under the Ministry of Economy and Finance, based on three decrees published in the official journal Le Moniteur on 21 August. The authority will license and supervise casinos, betting and borlette lottery banks and is tasked with fighting money laundering. Licence payments must go solely through the tax office DGI; trade press reports a 5% monthly levy on GGR and an annual online licence fee of 5 million gourdes.

